{
  "text": " The nonprofit Feds for Medical Freedom has just won a big court victory against mandating the COVID vaccines for federal employees and contractors. And we have the president and co-founder of Feds for Medical Freedom, Marcus Thornton, here to tell us about this important court decision. First, if I could, I'd like to give just a little bit of brief background on our organization. We're a grassroots nonprofit organization, a coalition of over 8,000 federal employees and contractors who don't believe that our government can or should compel us to get vaccinated or disclose our vaccination status. We believe that to do so is not only immoral but unconstitutional. We feel strongly about this and we're motivated by our personal religious beliefs, our beliefs in the Constitution, our opposition to government-backed oppression, and a conviction about our right to bodily autonomy and medical freedom. This was great news for our organization. It's something that we've been working towards for a while and, you know, all the credit goes to our awesome attorneys. This gives us the opportunity to have our day in court. The court said that our case would be heard by the full Fifth Circuit en banc, which is the full panel of, I believe, 17 federal judges, the week of September 12th, so later this year. And, you know, we're looking forward to it. We're looking forward to our attorneys having the opportunity to present the facts and, you know, I'm confident that right will prevail. Yeah, great. So tell me, what does it mean between now and then for you all? Well, it means that for now the injunction that was issued by the federal judge in Galveston remains in place, which means that federal employees are protected from the vaccine mandate until the Fifth Circuit chooses to make a decision on this. Okay, awesome. And the date is September. When will they be going back? Yeah, it'll be the week of September 12th. We don't have an exact date yet, but sometime mid-September. Okay, awesome. Well, we will be rooting for you. We're so excited that this is the case that gives you some more months and just thrilled about the decision. So I know you are too. Thank you so much for being with us. As are we. If anybody wants to learn more about organization or, you know, they want to see the case filing itself, they can go to our website. And that's www.feds4 and that's the number four medfreedom.org.",
